{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":484497,"name":"Panda","username":"grokpanda","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/53a042/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-06T11:26:11.046Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEquipment: Macbook Air M1\u003cbr\u003e\nMacOS version: Tahoe 26.5\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot Info:\u003cbr\u003e\nVersion: 0.43.0\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: darwin\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday, Sep 6, my Grok Bot lost connection to the computer. I tried all retries, updates and resets. See results below.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetry connecting:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Reconnecting…” for about a minute.\u003cbr\u003e\nThen, “Couldn’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer. Your Bots, files, and logins are safe. If it doesn’t reconnect on its own, recover Grok Bot’s computer to keep the data.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Update failed. The update couldn’t finish. Agent Computer is still on its previous image. Your files and logins are kept; installed apps and packages are not. Any agent turn that cannot pause is discarded”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecover my computer:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Recover failed. The recovery couldn’t finish, so Grok Bot’s computer may still be unreachable. Your Bots, files, and logins are safe.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetry Recovery:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Recover failed. The recovery couldn’t finish, so Grok Bot’s computer may still be unreachable. Your Bots, files, and logins are safe.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReset:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Reset failed. The reset couldn’t finish. Grok Bot’s computer may be in a partial state – retry to run the reset again.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetry reset:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Reset failed. The reset couldn’t finish. Grok Bot’s computer may be in a partial state – retry to run the reset again.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso tried resetting via smartphone app, but no success.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow the steps described above.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProvided above\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-06T11:26:19.365Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":32,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":162.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170775,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset","display_username":"Panda","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136423,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset/170775/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true,"can_vote":false},{"id":484517,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-06T11:54:40.739Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. Good news: your Grok Bot computer and Bots are fine, they’re working on our side and nothing is lost. You don’t need Reset, Recover, or Update here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a known issue on 0.43.0: if your Cursor password was recently changed or reset, or you signed out on another device, it signs out all devices. The 0.43.0 desktop app keeps the old session and, instead of asking you to sign in again, shows Couldn’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer. For the same reason, Update, Recover, and Reset fail too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFix: just sign out and sign back in in the desktop app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Grok Bot on Mac, click your name or avatar at the bottom left of the sidebar.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChoose Sign out and confirm.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign in again with the same Cursor account you used to create your Bots, using your new password. If you have multiple Cursor accounts, make sure you pick the right one.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait about a minute. Your Bots should load.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you don’t see Sign out in the menu, right-click the Grok Bot icon in the menu bar, choose Quit, reopen the app, and try again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if it still won’t connect after signing in again.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-06T11:54:40.739Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":36.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":170775,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset/170775/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":true,"topic_accepted_answer":true},{"id":485669,"name":"Aleks E","username":"Aleks_E","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/3be4f8/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T18:08:30.575Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi Dean, I have a similar issue, but signing out and signing back in has not restored access.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy existing Grok Bot computer first showed a connection error involving *.cursorvm.com. After signing out and signing back in, the client now shows both:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e“Reconnecting to your computer…”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e“No saved Bots yet”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is blocking access to my existing Bots and computer. Please escalate this to the team that can inspect the account-to-computer mapping and reattach the existing Grok Bot computer / backend association to my account, if that association is missing or incorrect. Please verify the original computer and its stored data before making any changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe cause is not yet confirmed. Please also check for an account/session mismatch and explain how I can securely verify that this is the original account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease preserve the existing computer, Bots, files, logins and history. I do not authorize Reset, Recover, Update Computer, deletion, replacement/provisioning of a new computer, or creation of new Bots as part of this request. Please ask me before any action that could alter or discard existing state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease provide a private official support channel where I can supply the account identifier, exact hostname, request ID, timestamps and diagnostics if needed. I have left those details out of this public reply.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCan you help restore access to the existing computer and confirm the next non-destructive step?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T18:08:30.575Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170775,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset","display_username":"Aleks E","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136673,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset/170775/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true},{"id":485704,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T18:44:30.233Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the details. Your case is different from the original one in this thread. In that case, re-login helps, but for you it didn’t, plus you’re seeing No saved Bots yet and the \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e error. That’s a different scenario where an existing computer doesn’t reattach to the account after signing in.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost important point. Your Grok Bot computer, Bots, files, and logins are saved on our side, nothing is lost. We won’t do any Reset, Recover, Update, or provision a new computer. This needs to be checked at the account-to-computer mapping level, not fixed on the client. This is an issue we’re tracking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo look into your specific account, we need details that you shouldn’t post publicly. Please email \u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e and include:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe account email that was used to create the Bots, if you have multiple accounts, please specify which one\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe Request ID in the app right top corner of the chat \u0026gt; Copy Request ID\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eapproximate timestamps for when access was lost, with timezone\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe exact computer hostname, if you have it\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith that info, the team can check the original computer and its data before making any changes. Once you’ve sent it, let me know here so I can keep an eye on it.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T18:44:30.233Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170775,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":136673,"username":"Aleks_E","name":"Aleks E","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/3be4f8/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset/170775/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true}],"stream":[484497,484517,485669,485704]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,2],[3,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot lost connection with its computer and can\u0026rsquo;t update/recover/reset","id":170775,"title":"Grok Bot lost connection with its computer and can't update/recover/reset","posts_count":4,"created_at":"2026-09-06T11:26:10.990Z","views":69,"reply_count":2,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-07T18:44:30.233Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset","category_id":6,"word_count":933,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":136423,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":null,"slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_170775","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":7,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":10,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":7,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false}],"chunk_size":20,"bookmarked":false,"topic_timer":{"id":31950,"execute_at":"2026-09-09T18:44:30.233Z","duration_minutes":2880,"based_on_last_post":true,"status_type":"close","category_id":null},"message_bus_last_id":26,"participant_count":3,"show_read_indicator":false,"thumbnails":null,"slow_mode_enabled_until":null,"tags_disable_ads":false,"related_topics":[{"fancy_title":"Unable to reconnect to my Grok Bot\u0026rsquo;s computer after attempted update","id":170000,"title":"Unable to reconnect to my Grok Bot's computer after attempted update","slug":"unable-to-reconnect-to-my-grok-bots-computer-after-attempted-update","posts_count":3,"reply_count":0,"highest_post_number":9,"image_url":"